{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T09:01:04.439Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"a4b3b83fd9ccfcf2d934c5f6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T09:01:04.439Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"The initial 100-subscriber/10-writer trial stopped: 50/50 commits, 7 missing CLI facts at every subscriber (700 missing deliveries), zero duplicates, complete-write p99 3942.2 ms. A second 20-subscriber/5-writer audit missed 2 CLI facts while every committed update remained readable in the derived event index. No measured server CPU, event-loop, memory or PostgreSQL connection limit explained this. Added a deterministic separate-real-CLI regression proving an older-timestamp fact is skipped behind the SDK exclusive cursor. The bounded production repair replays a 60-second inclusive window, dedupes item/version, preserves receipts across read-error restarts, and explicitly errors at 10000 retained facts per active project. No SDK pin or upstream source changed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T09:01:04.439Z"}],"before_hash":"456bbe6c36ead536c40d6dba75c46ee186996862539e294dad3429ab73c5c805","after_hash":"fb410549278643070cc0d9874d50d6d6d377cf5882ba528689d0b4e524594050","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5c3a451331196f339d019afa183b8c554bae90ea6b7bca2